From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: URL checks, content protection check, profile manager version, writer configuration

Stubs (FIXME / E_NOTIMPL / semi-stub), as documented now.

- WMCheckURLExtension: S_OK when the extension of the file name (the last
  dot of the last path component, leaving out a query or fragment, any
  case) is asf, wm, wma, wmv or mp3, NS_E_INVALID_NAME otherwise; it
  answered NS_E_INVALID_NAME for everything. The conformance test's
  todo_wine for these is removed. WMCheckURLScheme: S_OK for file, http,
  mms, mmst, mmsu, rtsp, rtspt, rtspu.
- WMIsContentProtected (always FALSE before) reads the ASF header of the file
  and looks for a content encryption or extended content encryption object
  (GUIDs from the ASF specification): S_OK with TRUE when there is one,
  S_FALSE with FALSE otherwise or when the file cannot be read.
- IWMProfileManager2: Get/SetSystemProfileVersion (default 8.0, the four
  versions 4.0, 7.0, 8.0, 9.0 are valid) and the argument checks of the
  calls that need profile objects, which this implementation does not have
  (they stay E_NOTIMPL once the arguments are valid).
- IWMWriterAdvanced / IWMWriterAdvanced2 / IWMWriterAdvanced3: sync
  tolerance (default 3000 ms), SetLiveSource / IsRealTime, SetNonBlocking,
  and the sink list (GetSinkCount, GetSink, AddSink, RemoveSink, holding a
  reference on every sink). The writer object was not zero-initialised.

